{"id": "EUVD-2026-82187", "enisaUuid": "0ad312fd-e874-3eef-bae3-476a1b64c69f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncxl/features: Clamp Get Feature output size to the remaining buffer\n\ncxl_get_feature() reads a feature in a loop but passes a fixed size_out\nas the output capacity every iteration. On the last partial iteration\nthe buffer has less room left, so a device that returns more than asked\ncan overflow feat_out.\n\nUse the per-iter size data_to_rd_size, which already tracks the\nremaining room, as the output capacity.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8abbd5c2928fd839dab702244cc57b228ab43aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca95b15a0760e7724e61addbdd61050be13b6406", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aeb21fe557ef154f0cdf4f9745ebd8d5b31ca83"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93077", "GHSA-qp96-h2xq-qgj3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "41cd06b2-88bd-3ba7-bcbe-de1266bc99b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e5ac21f629de796ab5d598b59c5e468c6fe4f95 <b8abbd5c2928fd839dab702244cc57b228ab43aa"}, {"id": "7ff53de6-a6c8-369a-931c-0bf0aee4d29f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "817b4e27-2b4d-3d81-bec0-d5b809ec0ae0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "93a6a8dd-425b-3bb2-957b-c7d794811980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d7f2f870-f853-31b9-83f1-5a509f1ce707", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e5ac21f629de796ab5d598b59c5e468c6fe4f95 <2aeb21fe557ef154f0cdf4f9745ebd8d5b31ca83"}, {"id": "e1daf682-b0e4-38fa-88a7-364bf316bac8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5